  "denomination": {
    "note": "Amounts are public for a subset of notes, and only a subset. Two routes expose them: an open note publishes note_id and OpenNoteDeposited publishes the same note_id with an amount (exact join), or the note's transaction carries exactly one distinct deposit amount. A change note minted by spending an existing note has neither, so its amount is unobservable and is left unknown. EncNoteCreated.packed_value was tested and does not carry the amount. The candidate set is the observable same-denomination set: the notes an adversary can actually list. Change notes are not in it, and not because they were excluded for convenience — they are created by a spend rather than a deposit, so they are structurally distinguishable from a note whose amount is known.",
